HOW TO DEPLOY TO PRODUCTION
---------------------------

# Explicit file list -- do NOT go back to `sudo cp ~/dokimion/config/production/dokimion/* .`
# That wildcard also copied dokimion-production.key into sites-available, which IS
# security_hardening_production.md finding H2 (needless world-readable copy of the
# shared upstream private key on the load balancer). It also dumped nginx.conf,
# nginx.service, rsyslog.conf, rsyslog.service and this README into a directory
# where none of them belong; those four have their own destinations, see
# config/common/install_configfiles.py.

# ==> load_balancer.conf IN THIS DIRECTORY IS SHARED WITH STAGING. <==
# It is the ONLY copy in the repo, and the staging LB installs it from here too
# (config/staging/s-dokimion/README does the same). So an edit made here for production
# reaches s-dokimion.psonet as well, and this path is the one that bites: nothing in this
# directory's name suggests staging depends on it. Keep anything environment-specific in the
# .h includes -- those ARE per-LB (servers.h, certificates.h, server_name.h, proxy_pass.h,
# http_return.h, rate_limiting.h, lb_client_cert.h). The same applies to
# production/dokimion1/dokimion_common.conf, which all six web servers share.

R=~/dokimion/config/production/dokimion
sudo install -m 644 -t /etc/nginx/sites-available \
  $R/load_balancer.conf $R/servers.h $R/certificates.h $R/server_name.h \
  $R/rate_limiting.h $R/proxy_pass.h $R/http_return.h $R/lb_client_cert.h

# VERIFY THE INSTALL LANDED, BEFORE RELOADING. A failed `install` leaves the previous valid
# config in place, so `nginx -t` passes and the reload succeeds while nothing has changed --
# no warning, every signal healthy. This exact no-op cost 3.5 hours on dokimion3 during the
# mTLS rollout (mtls_h1_deploy.md) and six days of live wildcard CORS on s-dokimion1
# (security_hardening_staging.md, M1 + L4). A single source file is NOT evidence that the
# server received it.
md5sum /etc/nginx/sites-available/load_balancer.conf $R/load_balancer.conf   # must match

sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx

# Certificates are deliberately NOT part of this sync -- they are already installed
# on the box. If rebuilding the LB from scratch, install dokimion-production.crt
# (mode 644, needed for proxy_ssl_trusted_certificate) and the client-facing
# testing_languagetechnology_org.pem/.key referenced by certificates.h. Do not put
# dokimion-production.key on the LB at all; the LB never presents it.
